{
  "description": "#5841 S4 — `rename_property_option` renames the harness space's `stage` option `review` to `in_review` in place, keeping the options' order, and every value of the space equal to it, the trashed card's included, in one `rename_property_option` op. `draft` (another option) and `done` (held by `four`, no longer an option) are untouched. Refused, in this order: a built-in key (`BuiltinPropertyLocked`), a key the app writes itself, a blank new name, a rename onto itself, an undeclared key (not_found), a non-select key, an old name that is not an option, a new name that is already an option, and one a block holds; a refusal appends nothing. `undo_ops` renames back, which the second rename relies on: it finds `review` an option again. Once `review` is an option again, undoing the second rename is refused. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
